{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1297a97530c4f35c3178146d49cc1b374257d48a5ea11d2d886ba5c376c3e0c7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is described as a collection of 16 specialized AI coding agents, each designed around a Myers-Briggs personality type to offer distinct approaches to software development challenges."},{"claim_ids":["clm_409507ef3f7ca6b46b71f5ed4e9e3c5c7333d920ca4d1320808c001a5f891280"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README claims bilingual support, providing analysis in Chinese and English."},{"claim_ids":["clm_43256bd1a511301b6a167572c49d2680c08d862ae148eefa9f82cadc45baf3cb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README documents slash commands including /squad for team selection, /battle [task] [report] for agent competition, /my-coding-mbti for coding-pattern analysis, and /output-style [style] for personality-tuned output."},{"claim_ids":["clm_587de6c3d9a6220bb7943b1e9cef4eedaa2c3ed6e55dfb79e4e2a194e351cd08"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README advertises multi-dimensional project evaluation described as balanced analysis, alongside the 16 personality agents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9b6a21dd19cdb3fead9abc5e06971ef8f3b928c2c700df100d6963c93b6cacb3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installation is documented as cloning the GitHub repository, entering the directory, and running npm run install."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b55694aa9292bc4c85687c1de0479fd64a16219c3438dc60b97042fc161ddad9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agents are grouped into four MBTI categories: Analysts (NT), Diplomats (NF), Sentinels (SJ), and Explorers (SP), each listing four specific types such as INTJ, INFP, ESTJ, and ESFP."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e1d167e97b4261f5fd746ccf0d8cc3e2bc855d7e12cf51aeceda7541a5f716de"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README itself is provided in eight languages: English, Chinese, Japanese, Portuguese (BR), French, German, Korean, and Arabic, each repeating the same feature and category descriptions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f995f17f10bbd53aefb4c1c0d1802777100d5a65724189639c80407a5714ffa0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The design philosophy states the project was motivated by bridging communication gaps between personality types, with agents embodying different cognitive styles to fill blind spots and expand the toolkit."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f9bdc52c9d99326662f9e02578e55ad0aaefc40e03d72313f4a7159dace34a87"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The slash-command style (/squad, /battle, /my-coding-mbti, /output-style) suggests the agents are intended for use within a Claude-style command-driven coding environment, though no runtime code is shown in the evidence."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1297a97530c4f35c3178146d49cc1b374257d48a5ea11d2d886ba5c376c3e0c7","clm_409507ef3f7ca6b46b71f5ed4e9e3c5c7333d920ca4d1320808c001a5f891280","clm_43256bd1a511301b6a167572c49d2680c08d862ae148eefa9f82cadc45baf3cb","clm_587de6c3d9a6220bb7943b1e9cef4eedaa2c3ed6e55dfb79e4e2a194e351cd08","clm_9b6a21dd19cdb3fead9abc5e06971ef8f3b928c2c700df100d6963c93b6cacb3","clm_b55694aa9292bc4c85687c1de0479fd64a16219c3438dc60b97042fc161ddad9","clm_e1d167e97b4261f5fd746ccf0d8cc3e2bc855d7e12cf51aeceda7541a5f716de","clm_f995f17f10bbd53aefb4c1c0d1802777100d5a65724189639c80407a5714ffa0","clm_f9bdc52c9d99326662f9e02578e55ad0aaefc40e03d72313f4a7159dace34a87"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_b86854b4592a4980b4b412b11db03f39","id":"pg_9fcebb1f6ecb5d8c9acdab62fce41b9e","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/weiyangzen-mbti-coding-agents-readme-md-964e157ac85a-ab62fce41b9e.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_09dfb4cfbab152faa6579c2e094d1cb5"],"title":"weiyangzen/mbti-coding-agents/README.md @ 964e157ac85a","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b86854b4592a4980b4b412b11db03f39"}
